# The release machine's identity. On Mac copy to
# artifacts/release-work/release.env in the repository and fill in.
# Windows and Linux use ~/.umbratic/release.env.
# `npm run desktop:release` and the Veil Console release command load it.
# Keep it readable by you alone (chmod 600); never commit it.
#
# Values on the command line win over this file. Quotes around a value are
# allowed and stripped.

# --- Optional server web search ---------------------------------------------
# The self-hosting operator's Brave Search API credential. The server release
# command embeds it into Veil; it does not belong to the desktop renderer.
# Leave empty for a deployment without web search. Search limits are operator
# policy, configured by the release command's --searches-per-month option.
UMBRATIC_BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=

# --- macOS: notarization ----------------------------------------------------
# Import a Developer ID Application certificate with its private key into your
# keychain, or set CSC_LINK (P12 path/base64) and CSC_KEY_PASSWORD.
# Choose ONE complete notarization credential set.
APPLE_ID=
APPLE_APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD=
APPLE_TEAM_ID=
# Alternative App Store Connect API credentials:
# APPLE_API_KEY=/absolute/path/to/AuthKey_XXXXXXXXXX.p8
# APPLE_API_KEY_ID=
# APPLE_API_ISSUER=

# --- Windows distribution signing -------------------------------------------
# SignPath signing runs only in the approved GitHub-hosted release workflow.
# Configure SIGNPATH_ORGANIZATION_ID, SIGNPATH_PROJECT_SLUG,
# SIGNPATH_SIGNING_POLICY_SLUG and SIGNPATH_PUBLISHER as Actions variables, and
# SIGNPATH_API_TOKEN as an Actions secret used only by the official Action.
# Do not put that token in this file. Local Windows inspection uses --unsigned.
# See docs/guides/release-desktop.md and CODE_SIGNING_POLICY.md.
